r a shift in Latino turnout patterns in San Antonio could break the race decisively toward either candidate.", "confidence": "low", "notes": []}, "overview": "Texas's 35th District is an open seat redrawn by Republicans to be more favorable, yet it has become one of the cycle's most competitive House races. Republican Carlos De La Cruz and Democrat Johnny Garcia have each raised roughly a million dollars, with heavy outside spending on both sides. Trump has campaigned in San Antonio to rally Republicans, underscoring how contested the seat is.\n\nExpert ratings are split: several call it Lean R, while others rate it a Tossup and one rates it Lean D. Prediction markets lean toward Garcia at about 60 percent. The only available poll, from August, showed a one-point Republican edge. With thin polling and conflicting signals, the race sits at a coin flip with a modest Democratic edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4325, "margin": -0.99}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5895, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6117, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6193, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5254, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5283, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5907, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6027, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6095, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5948, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.596, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.5662, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.594, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.527, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.539, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3993, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3992, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.4712, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.5262, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_de